{{!
    @template theme_nit/auth_mode_toggle

    The light/dark switch on the account screens (log in, sign up), drawn in the
    utility line beside the language menu. Rendered as a partial from
    theme_nit/core/loginform and theme_nit/core/signup_form_layout, with the
    context theme_nit\output\core_renderer::auth_mode_toggle_context() builds.

    It is the navbar's switch (theme_nit/navbar_mode_toggle) in the shape of
    that line: the same data attributes, the same click handler and the same
    cookie, so a mode chosen here is the mode the site opens in after log-in.
    Only the look differs — the log-in layout has no navigation bar, and the
    utility line is a row of small text controls ("English (en)", "Access as a
    guest"), so this is a text button with a glyph rather than the bar's bare
    42px icon.

    The glyph and the word both name the mode the button switches TO, the way
    the bar's does: a moon and "Dark mode" while the page is light, a bulb and
    "Light mode" while it is dark. Both halves are in the markup and CSS shows
    the one that applies, keyed off `data-nit-mode` (the rule sits with the
    bar's in _navbar.scss, `.nit-mode-toggle`), so the label follows the
    attribute the handler already flips and the server-rendered first paint is
    right with no script at all. No visually-hidden copy of the label: the
    accessible name is the aria-label, which the handler rewrites on each click.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * mode - the mode currently showing, "light" or "dark"
    * label - accessible name: the mode the button switches TO
    * config - JSON for the click handler; see theme_nit/navbar_mode_toggle

    Example context (json):
    {
        "mode": "light",
        "label": "Switch to dark mode",
        "config": "(the JSON described in theme_nit/navbar_mode_toggle)"
    }
}}
<button type="button" class="btn nit-auth-utility-btn nit-mode-toggle nit-auth-mode-toggle"
        data-nit-mode-toggle data-nit-mode="{{mode}}" data-nit-mode-config="{{config}}"
        title="{{label}}" aria-label="{{label}}">
    <i class="icon fa fa-moon fa-fw nit-mode-icon nit-mode-icon-dark" aria-hidden="true"></i>
    <i class="icon fa fa-lightbulb fa-fw nit-mode-icon nit-mode-icon-light" aria-hidden="true"></i>
    <span class="nit-mode-text nit-mode-text-dark">{{#str}} modedark, theme_nit {{/str}}</span>
    <span class="nit-mode-text nit-mode-text-light">{{#str}} modelight, theme_nit {{/str}}</span>
</button>
